{"reference":"Isaiah 57","book":"Isaiah","chapter":57,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Isaiah in Ancient Manuscripts","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Isaiah 57 belongs to a book preserved in the Great Isaiah Scroll, an almost complete ancient copy of all sixty-six chapters. It broadly agrees with the Masoretic tradition while also containing many spelling and substantive differences. Other Qumran manuscripts and interpretive writings show that Isaiah was actively copied and interpreted; the significance of particular differences remains disputed.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_057_3e93eca5d4ffd2ac5c85f0d0"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}